{"parentUuid":"404dcf63-a778-4c83-b641-7b971dd5d5a8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgr9HaZ1iNdUZcxTrBp7v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"For a Cloudflare Worker, which is what this repo uses, the fetch handler should be a thin entry point that catches errors and delegates routing to a separate function:\n\n```ts\nexport interface Env {\n  DB: D1Database;\n  API_TOKEN: string;\n}\n\nexport default {\n  async fetch(request: Request, env: Env, ctx: ExecutionContext): Promise<Response> {\n    try {\n      return await route(request, env, ctx);\n    } catch (err) {\n      console.error('unhandled', err);\n      return json({ error: 'internal_error' }, 500);\n    }\n  },\n} satisfies ExportedHandler<Env>;\n\nasync function route(request: Request, env: Env, ctx: ExecutionContext): Promise<Response> {\n  const url = new URL(request.url);\n  if (request.method === 'OPTIONS') return preflight();\n  if (request.method === 'GET' && url.pathname === '/health') return json({ ok: true });\n  if (request.method === 'POST' && url.pathname === '/items') return createItem(request, env, ctx);\n  return json({ error: 'not_found' }, 404);\n}\n```\n\nThe main points:\n\n- **One default export with `fetch(request, env, ctx)`.** Bindings and secrets come from `env`, never from module-level globals. Request-specific state stays out of module scope.\n- **Route early and return early.** Handle CORS preflight and health checks before any real work. Keep each route in its own function that takes the request and returns a `Response`.\n- **Wrap the whole dispatch in one try/catch.** Log the error server-side and return a generic JSON error. Don't send stack traces to the client.\n- **Use `ctx.waitUntil()` for work that can finish after the response,** such as logging or analytics. Don't await it on the request path.\n- **Set timeouts on outbound calls** with `AbortSignal.timeout(...)` so a slow upstream can't hold the request open.\n- **Stream proxied bodies** by passing `response.body` through rather than buffering it.\n\nThe same shape applies to other edge runtimes, but the export differs. Vercel Edge Functions use a named or default export of a handler function, and Supabase Edge Functions call `Deno.serve(handler)`. If you meant one of those, tell me and I'll adjust the example."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5339,"cache_read_input_tokens":16614,"output_tokens":1773,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1015},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5339,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1773,"cache_read_input_tokens":16614,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5339,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5339},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestedModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"11b8e2e9-87c7-45b0-93c6-c981f1820390","timestamp":"2026-11-08T21:07:47.440Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionId":"8c48d12e-ea9d-49ce-9d1d-e09ca732b504","version":"2.1.319"}
